diabetes-detection
==================

This repository contains a failed attempt at diabetes detection using mathematical models.
Prediabetes, Type 1 diabetes, Type 2 diabetes, and Pancreatic diabetes were the targets of the prediction.
XGBoost and Random Forest models both showed nearly equal efficiency.
The attempt also focused on using a dual layer approach : One smaller dataset that judges the presence of diabetes and a larger dataset for classification.

Finding a exotic and genuine dataset large enough for the job was almost impossible.
Hence, a synthetic dataset has been used for the second layer.

However, the quantity and quality of data required for such an undertaking is just too much.
This was further compounded by my lack of complete understanding of the models I was using. As I moved to fields with lesser code abstraction, my interest in this project waned.

Hopefully, this repository can become a starting point for others who wish to continue.
Feel free to fork this repository and use it in any way you see fit.

All the best,
Subramanya J